; Scrub — NEW TerrainDefinition (habitat-tiers ruling, 2026-09-04 -> task-8-brief.md).
; VALUES BELOW ARE A PROPOSAL AWAITING HUMAN SIGN-OFF (same posture as every other
; terrain's cost/scale/model choices in this codebase; see barn.tres for the same
; convention on the buildings side).
;
; WHY IT EXISTS: the second grazing terrain. `browse` vs `open_grass` is the real
; ecological browser/grazer split, which is what separates Donkey and the Deer herd tier
; from every grass-eater. It is also the "wild grass with tags" the human described —
; wild_grass.tres itself stays deliberately inert and is NOT changed by this task; the
; inert-land invariant (spec.md -> Shared Patterns) is untouched.
;
; emitted_tags = ["browse", "rocks"] is DECIDED by the habitat-tiers ruling
; (task-8-brief.md's table). No radius, no weight, no threshold — the v1 tag model
; (-> D-25) applies unchanged. `rocks` reuses the same tag Rock already emits (terrain.md);
; Scrub is a second, distinct source for it, not a duplicate declaration in the schema
; sense — each terrain still just lists what it emits.
;
; cost = 0 — natural terrain, "nature is free" (terrain.md's one pricing rule, unchanged by
; this task).
;
; MODEL_SCENE: Scrub.tscn (CC0, Ultimate Nature Pack + Stylized Nature MegaKit) — see that
; scene's own header for full sourcing/scale detail. Single variant; a multi-variant
; look-pass is out of scope here, same posture Grass/Rock/Wild grass all started with
; before their own later passes.
;
; PLAYER-VISIBLE CONSEQUENCE: Scrub is a new, free-to-paint entry in the Terraform
; palette — flagged prominently per this task's brief, not buried in a count bump.
;
; No `fact_text` copy yet — Content Pipeline step 5 (Content Writer), explicitly out of
; scope for this task.
; GRASS-FAMILY REWORK (2026-09-08), model_scenes 1 -> 3, applying the Grass calibration
; baseline. Variants: Scrub (rocky), ScrubBrush (browse-heavy, no rock) and ScrubSparse
; (thinnest cover, most bare ground). All 3 equal weight in pick_variant().
;
; ROCK SOURCE SWAPPED OFF THE ULTIMATE NATURE PACK onto the MegaKit (Rock_Medium_1/2,
; Pebble_Round_1/2), so this terrain no longer mixes packs inside a single tile — it was the
; only terrain that did. The 0.220 tile-unit rock target is carried over from what the old
; Rock_1 already measured to, so the swap changes the pack and not the size.
;
; BUSH SWAPPED Bush_Common_Flowers -> Bush_Common on the tag-partition rule: `flowers` is
; Meadow's tag and Meadow is its only source, so a flowering shrub on a `browse`/`rocks`
; terrain undercuts the partition. Bush_Common_Flowers stays imported on disk, unwired.
;
; ONE VARIANT CARRIES NO ROCK AT ALL (ScrubBrush) and that is safe: `emitted_tags` is read from
; THIS FILE, never from which variant a tile happens to draw, so `rocks` is unaffected.
;
; NO PICKER CONSEQUENCE — `scrub` is not a style-picker category. See meadow.tres.
;
; 5 NEW IMPORTS, MegaKit, CC0 1.0, audit gate re-checked: Bush_Common, Rock_Medium_1,
; Rock_Medium_2, Pebble_Round_1, Pebble_Round_2. All new scales are FIRST-PASS PROPOSALS.
[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="TerrainDefinition" load_steps=5 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/definitions/terrain_definition.gd" id="1_schema"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/terrain/scrub/Scrub.tscn" id="2_model"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/terrain/scrub_brush/ScrubBrush.tscn" id="3_model"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/terrain/scrub_sparse/ScrubSparse.tscn" id="4_model"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_schema")
id = "scrub"
display_name = "Scrub"
emitted_tags = Array[String](["browse", "rocks"])
cost = 0
model_scenes = Array[PackedScene]([ExtResource("2_model"), ExtResource("3_model"), ExtResource("4_model")])
harvestable = null
